From 33bc4f1f0ed0e22f92c17af9e19388dc530a6ea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:34:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] PS2 GS: trivial reject before building colour and UV

DrawVertices built every vertex in full (position, texture coordinates,
colour) before clipping, even for vertices that only belong to triangles
rejected because all three are outside the same plane. MakeVertex is now
split into SetPosition (clip position, one matrix product) and
SetAttributes (UV and colour).

DrawVertices runs four passes:
1. position and outcode for every vertex;
2. mark the vertices used by triangles that are not trivially rejected
   (same test as ClipEmit);
3. SetAttributes only for the marked vertices;
4. ClipEmit with the outcodes from pass 1, so each outcode is computed
   once per vertex. ClipAndEmit is kept as a wrapper.

The emitted triangles are the same: positions come from the same code,
attributes are computed the same way and only for vertices that are used.

Not measured. The gain depends on how many vertices of a draw are outside
the guard band; the extra pass costs a little when almost everything is
visible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yH2brr5GjCGyCE62bYyXR
---
